Since pre-registration starts tomorrow, I should probably get the
pre-announcement out today.  ;-)

Preparations for the Tournament are under way, but as usual are not
nearly as far along at this point as we'd like.  This year, unlike
previous years, it's less because I'm generally slothful and
interrupt-driven than because I took a day job this summer (don't feel
bad for me; it's a good job as an operations engineer at Twitter so I'm
pretty OK with it) and Jeri and I have a baby on the way too.  So prep
work is even slower than usual this time around.

I have settled on the new Challenge's structure and started work on the
patch; the only other new feature in the works is (surprise, surprise) a
bit of Twitter integration which allows the game servers to post to the
Tournament's Twitter account (http://twitter.com/devnull_nethack)
whenever a player dies and possibly on other significant character
events.  If Wolfgang rejoins us as an admin this year, we'll be running
an IRC bot again so I'll see that this integrates to IRC as well.

Over the next few weeks I will also be looking through the bug reports
and feature requests from last year, so hopefully we'll get some small
fixes in this year too.

The game server kit should be available for download on October 15th by
aspiring volunteer administrators.

See you all in two weeks.  ;-)

-robin


